* CABSRT12 - PRINT STREAM SORT FOR THE BURST SEQUENCE
* THE INSERTER TAKES THE PRINT STREAM IN MAIL SORT ORDER, NOT IN
* ACCOUNT ORDER.  THIS SORT PUTS IT IN ZIP CODE ORDER.  THE ORDER
* MATTERS TWICE OVER - THE ZIP GROUPS THE MAIL FOR THE INSERTER
* AND THE REST OF THE KEY HOLDS EACH INVOICE TOGETHER WITH ITS
* LINES IN THE SEQUENCE THE FORMATTER WROTE THEM.
*
* E15 EXIT CABSXZIP PULLS THE ZIP OFF THE INVOICE HEADER LINE,
* WHICH IS THE ONLY LINE IN THE STREAM THAT CARRIES IT, AND LAYS
* A TWENTY BYTE KEY OVER BYTES 1 TO 20 OF EVERY LINE.  E35 EXIT
* CABSXBST TAKES THAT KEY OFF AGAIN AND SUPPRESSES ANY DOCUMENT
* WHOSE FIRST LINE CARRIES A CARRIAGE CONTROL OTHER THAN 7.
*
* THIS SORT TAKES SORT, RECORD, MODS AND END AND NOTHING ELSE.
* THE EQUALS SETTING THE DFSORT CARD CARRIED IS GONE.  LINE ORDER
* INSIDE A DOCUMENT IS NOW HELD BY THE LINE ORDINAL THAT CABSXZIP
* BUILDS INTO THE KEY AND NOT BY THE SORT.
* THAT RULE IS NO LONGER VISIBLE ON THIS CARD.
 SORT FIELDS=(1,20,CH,A)
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=(133)
 MODS E15=(CABSXZIP,4096,SORTEXIT,N),E35=(CABSXBST,2048,SORTEXIT,N)
 END
